                <pb facs="0553" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/176: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-10T15:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:43 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>451. Department’s 297 September 29, 5 p.m. Foreign Office informs me that the
                    British High Commissioner at Constantinople and Minister at Athens are being
                    instructed to urge local representatives of British relief societies to
                    cooperate to the fullest possible extent with the American relief organizations
                    concerned.</p>
                <p>Above repeated to Constantinople and Athens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
